       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for 50 mg. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, this dose carries a real risk of serious harm, including profound hypotension and shock. It could also be hard to reverse, because amlodipine acts for a long time.\n\nHere are some options that could help with your timeline:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily right away. Titration can happen over the next days to weeks.\n- **Call pharmacy.** If you think this patient needs an unusual regimen, a pharmacist can review it with you quickly.\n- **Add a second agent.** If the goal is faster blood pressure control, you could use a different drug class or combination therapy instead of exceeding the maximum dose of one drug. I can enter that order if you tell me what you want.\n- **Get attending or cardiology input.** They can advise if the situation is unusual.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll enter it."
